Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:06.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Vision transformers are powerful but data-hungry: they only beat convolutional networks
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.44,0:00:09.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}when huge labeled datasets are available.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.23,0:00:11.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This paper introduces PatchRot,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.35,0:00:16.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a self-supervised technique crafted specifically for vision transformers.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.33,0:00:17.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The key idea is simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.90,0:00:23.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Rotate the whole image or its individual patches by multiples of ninety degrees,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.35,0:00:27.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and train the transformer to predict every rotation angle.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.31,0:00:32.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The class token predicts the image rotation, capturing global structure,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.22,0:00:37.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}while new per-patch heads predict each patch's rotation, capturing local detail.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.68,0:00:39.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}After this pretraining,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.25,0:00:46.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}PatchRot features consistently beat both supervised training from scratch and the RotNet baseline across CIFAR-10,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.03,0:00:49.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}CIFAR-100, FashionMNIST, and Tiny-ImageNet.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.26,0:00:55.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Vision transformers have overtaken convolutional networks on many vision tasks,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.33,0:00:58.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but only when trained on very large labeled datasets.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.73,0:01:02.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}With limited labels their performance falls behind ConvNets,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.58,0:01:08.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}because they lack built-in inductive biases like locality and translation equivariance.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.17,0:01:11.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Labeling data at the scale ViTs need is expensive and slow.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.95,0:01:16.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Self-supervised learning can help by learning useful features without labels,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.90,0:01:22.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but the popular self-supervised pretext tasks were all designed for convolutional networks
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.67,0:01:27.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and ignore the patch-token structure that makes transformers special.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.40,0:01:32.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A vision transformer splits an image into patches and applies self-attention,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.14,0:01:37.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so unlike a convolutional network it can produce a separate output for every patch,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.25,0:01:39.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}not just one output for the whole image.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.71,0:01:44.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Prior work called RotNet showed that simply predicting the rotation angle of an image
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.94,0:01:48.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}teaches a convolutional network surprisingly rich features.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.58,0:01:53.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The natural question is: can we push rotation prediction down to the patch level,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.56,0:01:59.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so the transformer learns local features for each patch as well as global structure for the whole image?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.97,0:02:04.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}That patch-level signal is exactly what a token-based model is built to exploit.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.19,0:02:08.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The paper makes three main contributions.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.92,0:02:12.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}First, it introduces PatchRot,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.64,0:02:16.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a self-supervised technique crafted for vision transformers that predicts rotation angles
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.37,0:02:20.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}at two levels: the class token predicts the whole-image rotation for global context,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.09,0:02:23.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and new per-patch heads predict each patch's rotation for local detail.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.82,0:02:27.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Second,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.54,0:02:31.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it introduces a buffer gap between patches during training so the network cannot cheat by matching continuous edges,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.27,0:02:34.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}forcing it to learn genuine content.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.00,0:02:38.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Third,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.72,0:02:42.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it demonstrates through extensive experiments that PatchRot beats both supervised training
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.45,0:02:46.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}from scratch and the RotNet baseline across multiple datasets,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.17,0:02:49.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and that its features transfer well and help in semi-supervised settings.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.20,0:02:51.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}PatchRot works as follows.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.85,0:02:55.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Take an input image and either rotate the whole image,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.27,0:02:57.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}or rotate each of its patches independently,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.06,0:03:03.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}by a random multiple of ninety degrees: zero, ninety, one-eighty, or two-seventy.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.19,0:03:09.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The vision transformer is then trained to predict these rotation angles as a simple four-way classification.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.03,0:03:14.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The transformer's class token, which normally predicts the object category,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.78,0:03:19.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}is repurposed to predict the whole-image rotation, capturing global structure.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.73,0:03:26.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}New multilayer-perceptron heads are attached to each patch token to predict that individual patch's rotation,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.63,0:03:28.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}capturing local detail.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.09,0:03:30.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}To prevent the network from cheating,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.44,0:03:34.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}patches are carved from a slightly larger grid and randomly cropped,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.74,0:03:40.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so a random buffer gap sits between them and edge continuity can't give away the answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.32,0:03:42.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Training happens at a reduced resolution;
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.92,0:03:48.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}then the extra patch heads are removed and the network is fine-tuned at full resolution
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.43,0:03:50.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}on the real classification task,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.46,0:03:54.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with positional embeddings interpolated to the larger patch count.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.94,0:04:00.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The authors test PatchRot on four standard image classification datasets: CIFAR-10,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.62,0:04:04.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}CIFAR-100, FashionMNIST at thirty-two by thirty-two resolution,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.93,0:04:08.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and Tiny-ImageNet at sixty-four by sixty-four.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.08,0:04:13.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}They also study SVHN and MNIST to probe rotation-invariant objects like digits.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.48,0:04:18.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The backbone is a compact vision transformer with six encoder blocks.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.21,0:04:23.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Patch sizes are four pixels for the small datasets and eight for Tiny-ImageNet,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.61,0:04:27.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with a buffer gap set to a quarter of the patch size.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.24,0:04:29.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Beyond plain classification,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.15,0:04:33.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}they evaluate transfer learning between CIFAR-10 and CIFAR-100,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.46,0:04:38.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and a semi-supervised setting on CIFAR-10 where only a handful of labels,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.46,0:04:42.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}from two hundred fifty up to ten thousand, are available.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.66,0:04:48.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The headline result is that PatchRot pretraining consistently outperforms both supervised
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.43,0:04:51.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}training from scratch and the RotNet rotation baseline,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.99,0:04:53.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}on every dataset tested.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.55,0:04:55.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On CIFAR-10 with full fine-tuning,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.75,0:04:59.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}PatchRot reaches ninety-two point six percent top-one accuracy,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.84,0:05:05.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}compared to eighty-three point nine percent for supervised training from scratch.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.08,0:05:12.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On CIFAR-100 the gap is even larger: seventy point six percent top-one versus fifty point two percent supervised,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.41,0:05:14.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and ninety point two percent top-five.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.87,0:05:20.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On FashionMNIST it improves ninety-four point one versus eighty-nine point eight.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.12,0:05:22.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Remarkably, even linear probing,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.20,0:05:26.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}where the entire network is frozen and only the final layer is trained,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.80,0:05:29.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}gets close to supervised performance,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.20,0:05:34.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and fine-tuning just a single encoder block already beats training from scratch.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.68,0:05:39.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The ablation study on CIFAR-10 confirms that every component of PatchRot matters.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.96,0:05:44.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Training on patch rotations alone, without whole-image rotation,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.14,0:05:49.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}drops accuracy to ninety-one point eight percent because the model loses global context.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.88,0:05:55.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Using only image rotation, essentially the RotNet approach adapted to a transformer,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.36,0:05:57.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}drops it to ninety-one point zero.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.58,0:06:01.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Rotating the image and its patches together in a single pass,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.56,0:06:04.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}rather than in separate passes, hurts performance,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.82,0:06:09.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}as does training at the original resolution instead of the reduced resolution,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.91,0:06:14.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and reusing the existing head instead of adding dedicated patch heads.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.48,0:06:19.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Each of these lands below the full method's ninety-two point six percent,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.24,0:06:21.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}showing every design decision contributes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.28,0:06:24.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The numbers tell a clear story.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.32,0:06:29.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On CIFAR-10, PatchRot reaches ninety-two point six percent top-one accuracy,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.31,0:06:34.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}an improvement of eight point seven points over supervised training from scratch.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.64,0:06:37.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On CIFAR-100 the improvement is over twenty points,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.99,0:06:41.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}from fifty point two to seventy point six percent top-one,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.80,0:06:44.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and ninety point two percent top-five.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.30,0:06:50.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}FashionMNIST improves to ninety-four point one percent and Tiny-ImageNet's top-five rises
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.14,0:06:52.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}to seventy-three point four percent.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.51,0:06:57.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In the semi-supervised setting with only four thousand labeled CIFAR-10 images,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.70,0:07:00.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}PatchRot reaches eighty-one percent accuracy,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.66,0:07:05.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}versus roughly fifty-four percent for supervised training on the same labels,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.72,0:07:10.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}showing how valuable the self-supervised features are when labels are scarce.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.08,0:07:13.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The takeaway is that a very simple idea,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.57,0:07:18.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}predicting the rotation of both the whole image and each individual patch,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.17,0:07:23.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}turns out to be a self-supervised task perfectly suited to vision transformers.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.09,0:07:28.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Because the class token learns global structure and the patch heads learn local detail,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.50,0:07:32.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}PatchRot teaches the transformer rich features without any labels,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.61,0:07:39.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and those features reliably beat supervised training from scratch and the RotNet baseline across four datasets,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.52,0:07:43.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}in transfer learning, and especially when labeled data is scarce.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.56,0:07:44.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It is a lightweight,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.81,0:07:49.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}practical recipe for pretraining vision transformers on limited data.
